  "meaning": "O Nappinnai, bride of Nandagopa's mighty son who never turns his shoulder in battle, fragrant-haired girl — open the door! The roosters have crowed everywhere and the koels coo on the jasmine bower. Come joyfully, your fine bangles ringing, to sing your husband's name."
 },
 {
  "n": 19,
  "title": "குத்து விளக்கெரிய",
  "titleEn": "The Lamplit Chamber",
  "raga": "Sahana",
  "tamil": [
